    title: "小型企業警惕網路攻擊：未修補的Windows伺服器與複雜的釣魚攻擊案例分析",
    summary: "本文透過兩起案例，強調了企業安全管理上的重大風險。第一例指出，一家小型建商因使用老舊且未修補的Windows伺服器，且備份設備與主機連線，導致被勒索軟體攻擊，無法恢復營運，最終破產。這突顯了即使是小型企業，也必須將備份資料離線或上雲端，並及時修補所有伺服器。第二例則描述了攻擊者如何透過入侵一家公司高管的電子郵件帳戶，發送高度擬真的釣魚郵件（RFP），並設置了電子郵件過濾規則，進行「中間人攻擊」（Man-in-the-middle）。攻擊者利用偽造的登入頁面，誘騙受害者輸入包含兩步驟驗證（2FA）的密碼，最終取得Microsoft 365帳戶的存取權。幸運的是，受害者使用了專門的軟體（TarBot），能偵測到異常登入行為，成功阻止了攻擊。專家建議，應採用抗釣魚的MFA方式，如硬體金鑰或Passkeys，來防禦AI輔助的釣魚攻擊。",
    tags: ["勒索軟體", "Windows伺服器", "釣魚攻擊", "中間人攻擊", "Microsoft 365", "MFA", "備份策略"],
    title_en: "Small Businesses Beware of Cyber Attacks: Case Studies of Unpatched Windows Servers and Sophisticated Phishing Attacks",
    summary_en: "This article highlights significant risks in corporate security management through two case studies. The first case points out that a small construction company, due to using an outdated and unpatched Windows server that was connected to its backup equipment, was hit by ransomware. The attack prevented the company from restoring operations, leading to its eventual bankruptcy. This underscores that even small businesses must keep backup data offline or in the cloud, and promptly patch all servers. The second case describes how attackers compromised a company executive's email account to send highly realistic phishing emails (RFP), and set up email filtering rules to execute a 'Man-in-the-middle' attack. The attackers used a fake login page to trick the victim into entering a password that included two-factor authentication (2FA), ultimately gaining access to the Microsoft 365 account. Fortunately, the victim used specialized software (TarBot) that detected the abnormal login behavior, successfully thwarting the attack. Experts recommend adopting anti-phishing MFA methods, such as hardware keys or Passkeys, to defend against AI-assisted phishing attacks.",
