    id: "20261008-15071",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "中國政府關聯駭客利用多種漏洞與自動化工具竊取全球敏感資料",
    summary: "美國網路安全機構CISA發布警示，指出中國政府關聯的網路威脅行為者，透過「Integrity Technology Group」等實體，正在結合自動化掃描工具、大型殭屍網路（botnets）和實體滲透技術，針對全球組織，包括美國關鍵基礎設施部門，竊取敏感資料。攻擊者利用多個已知的漏洞，例如針對Microsoft Exchange伺服器的跨站腳本（XSS）攻擊和密碼噴灑（password spraying），並透過VPN軟體建立持久性存取。他們會利用腳本竊取電子郵件和憑證。為減輕風險，組織應優先停用未使用的服務和連接埠，清理網頁應用程式輸入以防止注入攻擊，並為所有服務實施多因素驗證（MFA）。此外，應及時修補系統漏洞，以降低被攻陷的風險。文章列出了多個受影響的CVE編號，包括CVE-2014-6278、CVE-2015-3306等，建議組織應提升資安防禦層級。",
    tags: ["中國駭客", "CISA", "CVE-2014-6278", "Microsoft Exchange", "跨站腳本", "多因素驗證", "關鍵基礎設施"],
    title_en: "China-Linked Hackers Steal Global Sensitive Data Using Multiple Vulnerabilities and Automated Tools",
    summary_en: "The U.S. cybersecurity agency CISA has issued an alert, pointing out that China-linked threat actors, operating through entities such as 'Integrity Technology Group,' are targeting global organizations, including U.S. critical infrastructure sectors, to steal sensitive data. The attackers are combining automated scanning tools, large botnets, and physical penetration techniques. They exploit multiple known vulnerabilities, such as Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks and password spraying targeting Microsoft Exchange servers, and establish persistent access via VPN software. They use scripts to steal emails and credentials. To mitigate risks, organizations should prioritize disabling unused services and ports, sanitizing web application inputs to prevent injection attacks, and implementing Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) for all services. Furthermore, they should promptly patch system vulnerabilities to reduce the risk of compromise. The article lists multiple affected CVE IDs, including CVE-2014-6278 and CVE-2015-3306, and advises organizations to elevate their cybersecurity defenses.",
    tags_en: ["China Hackers", "CISA", "CVE-2014-6278", "Microsoft Exchange", "Cross-Site Scripting", "Multi-Factor Authentication", "Critical Infrastructure"],
