    title: "微軟報告揭露臺灣、日本國家級駭客活動激增，Google呼籲建立Hotpatch應對N-day漏洞",
    summary: "近期全球資安威脅態勢持續升溫，微軟發布的2026數位防禦報告指出，臺灣在過去一年間觀察到193起國家級駭客活動事件，影響程度排名全球第4名。此外，Google Project Zero警告，雖然零時差漏洞攻擊增加，但N-day漏洞遭利用速度加快才是當前主要的攻擊成長來源。為應對快速升溫的漏洞攻擊情勢，Google呼籲軟體業者不能僅依賴正式修補，更應建立Hotpatch等緊急應變機制，讓企業用戶能在等待正式修補期間降低曝險風險。在個資安全方面，多起事件如美珍香會員資料外洩，突顯企業在採用生成式AI輔助開發時，缺乏完整的治理、上線前測試及政策規範，導致個資風險外洩。此外，丹麥中央人口登記局（CPR）和一零四資訊科技等公司也因存取權限濫用或系統異常讀取，發生了大規模個資外洩事件。",
    tags: ["國家級駭客", "N-day漏洞", "Hotpatch", "生成式AI", "個資外洩", "微軟", "Google Project Zero"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Report Reveals Surge in State-Sponsored Hacking Activity Targeting Taiwan and Japan; Google Urges Hotpatch Implementation for N-day Vulnerabilities",
    summary_en: "The global cybersecurity threat landscape continues to escalate. Microsoft's 2026 Digital Defense Report indicates that Taiwan observed 193 state-sponsored hacking incidents over the past year, ranking it fourth globally in terms of impact. Furthermore, Google Project Zero warns that while zero-day vulnerability attacks are increasing, the primary source of current attack growth is the accelerated exploitation of N-day vulnerabilities. To address the rapidly escalating vulnerability attack situation, Google urges software vendors not to rely solely on official patches, but rather to establish emergency response mechanisms such as Hotpatch, allowing enterprise users to mitigate exposure risk while awaiting official patches. Regarding personal data security, multiple incidents, such as the Meizhenxiang member data leak, highlight that companies lack comprehensive governance, pre-deployment testing, and policy standards when adopting generative AI for development, leading to personal data leakage risks. Additionally, large-scale personal data leaks occurred involving the Danish Civil Registration System (CPR) and companies like 104 Information Technology due to excessive access privileges or anomalous system reading.",
