    summary: "資安廠商 SonicWall 發布警告，針對 SMA1000 用戶推出熱修補更新，修補一系列漏洞，包括 CVE-2026-102255、CVE-2026-102256、CVE-2026-102257 及 CVE-2026-102258 等。其中，CVE-2026-102255 的嚴重性尤為突出，CVSS 評分達到滿分 10 分，屬於預先身分驗證的伺服器請求偽造（SSRF）漏洞。此漏洞存在於 SMA1000 的 Appliance Work Place 介面，由於非預期的替代存取路徑，攻擊者可無需通過身分驗證，接觸內部功能並執行未經授權操作。SonicWall 強調用戶應儘速套用修補程式，因為過去該設備的重大漏洞（如 CVE-2026-15409、CVE-2026-83548）已被證實成為攻擊目標。由於缺乏其他替代緩解措施，建議用戶務必立即更新。",
    tags: ["SonicWall", "SMA1000", "CVE-2026-102255", "SSRF", "熱修補", "資安漏洞"],
    title_en: "SonicWall Issues Emergency Patch for SMA1000 Series Devices Addressing Multiple High-Risk Vulnerabilities, Including CVSS Max-Score SSRF Flaw",
    summary_en: "Cybersecurity vendor SonicWall has issued a hotfix update for SMA1000 users to patch a series of vulnerabilities, including CVE-2026-102255, CVE-2026-102256, CVE-2026-102257, and CVE-2026-102258. Of particular concern is CVE-2026-102255, which has a maximum CVSS score of 10 and is an unauthenticated Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability. This flaw resides in the SMA1000's Appliance Work Place interface. Due to an unexpected alternative access path, attackers can access internal functions and perform unauthorized operations without needing authentication. SonicWall emphasizes that users must apply the patch promptly, as the device has previously been targeted by major vulnerabilities (such as CVE-2026-15409 and CVE-2026-83548). Given the lack of alternative mitigation measures, users are strongly advised to update immediately.",
