    summary_en: "According to the IDC's Q3 2026 Global PC Shipment Report, the overall global PC market saw a year-over-year decline of 20.1%, reaching 62.7 million units. Although Apple shipped 5.9 million Macs in the quarter, representing an 11.3% drop year-over-year, Apple's market share in global PC shipments actually increased from 8.5% to 9.5% due to the larger overall market contraction. Among major competitors, Lenovo maintained the top spot, but HP experienced the largest year-over-year decline in shipments, reaching 30.9%. IDC pointed out that factors such as weak market demand, excess inventory, and economic slowdown may lead to promotional activities in the near future, but pricing is expected to remain high. The report predicts that overall economic weakness will make the market outlook dim for the remainder of 2026 and potentially into 2027.",
