    title: "參議員指控 Trump Mobile 缺乏 FCC 授權，國際通訊服務及客戶資料安全成疑",
    summary: "美國參議員 Maggie Hassan 在信函中指出，Trump Mobile 在提供國際通訊服務的部分，似乎未能取得必要的 FCC 授權。此外，該公司也未提交應對語音機器人電話（robocalls）的必要計畫。Hassan 的信件還提出多項安全疑慮，包括近期發生駭客竊取 3,615 位客戶個人資料的事件，以及公司過去曾確認其供應商暴露客戶資料的紀錄。參議員指出，Trump Mobile 在應對資料外洩時，曾回應「我們沒有處理此類事件的團隊」，且其服務啟用流程過於簡化，可能讓詐騙分子更容易取得美國號碼。Hassan 質疑，缺乏授權和不完善的資料安全機制，可能影響國家安全，並要求釐清其國際電信服務的提供方與授權依據。",
    tags: ["Trump Mobile", "FCC", "國際通訊", "資料外洩", "Maggie Hassan", "美國電信"],
    title_en: "Senator Accuses Trump Mobile of Lacking FCC Authorization for International Communications, Raising Concerns Over International Service and Customer Data Security",
    summary_en: "In a letter, U.S. Senator Maggie Hassan pointed out that Trump Mobile appears to lack the necessary FCC authorization for providing international communication services. Furthermore, the company has not submitted a required plan to address robocalls. Hassan's letter also raised multiple security concerns, including a recent incident where hackers stole the personal data of 3,615 customers, and the company's past acknowledgment of a supplier exposing customer data. The Senator noted that when responding to the data breach, Trump Mobile stated, 'We do not have a team to handle this type of incident,' and that its service activation process is overly simplified, potentially making it easier for scammers to acquire U.S. numbers. Hassan questioned that the lack of authorization and inadequate data security mechanisms could impact national security, and demanded clarification regarding the provider and authorization basis for its international telecommunications services.",
    tags_en: ["Trump Mobile", "FCC", "International Communications", "Data Breach", "Maggie Hassan", "U.S. Telecommunications"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/10/trump-mobile-doesnt-seem-to-have-fcc-authorization-for-phone-service-senator-says", lang: "EN" }
    ]
